<!-- Documentation: https://www.jetbrains.org/intellij/sdk/docs/basics/plugin_structure/plugin_configuration_file.html -->

<!-- url="" specifies the URL of the plugin homepage (displayed in the Welcome Screen and in "Plugins" settings dialog) -->
<idea-plugin url="https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/wikis">
    
    <!-- Unique identifier of the plugin. Cannot be changed between the plugin versions. If not specified, assumed to be equal to <name>. -->
    <id>net.javaru.idea.frc</id>
    <name>FRC</name>
    <version>replacedAtBuildTime</version>

    <!-- The vendor of the plugin.
       The optional "url" attribute specifies the URL of the vendor homepage.
       The optional "email" attribute specifies the e-mail address of the vendor. -->
    <vendor url="https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin" >Javaru</vendor>
    
    <!-- please see http://www.jetbrains.org/intellij/sdk/docs/basics/getting_started/build_number_ranges.html for description -->
    <!-- Minimum ('since-build') and maximum ('until-build') build of IDEA compatible with the plugin -->
    <idea-version since-build="*.*" until-build="*.*"/> 

    <description><![CDATA[
        <p>
            <!-- The first sentence gets used as a summary at the JetBrains Plugins Repository. -->
            <em><a href='http://www.firstinspires.org/'>FIRST</a> Robotics Competition</em>
            (<a href='http://www.firstinspires.org/robotics/frc'>FRC</a>) development support for
            IntelliJ IDEA, including new project wizards, new class templates, robust RioLog console,
            and more. Works with all v2019.2 or later editions (Community, Education, and Ultimate) 
            of IntelliJ IDEA. Enjoy using your favorite IDE when coding your team's robot in Java
            and/or Kotlin.
        </p>
        <p><br></p>
        <p>
            <strong>Please report issues or make feature requests via the project's</strong>
            <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues'>Issue Tracker</a>.<br>
            This is an unofficial plugin written by an FRC team mentor. Please do <em>not</em> 
            contact <em>FIRST</em> or the WPI Lib developers for support. Use the above link. Thanks.
        </p>        
    ]]></description>

    <change-notes><![CDATA[
        <strong>v1.3.0</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; This is a re-release of v1.2.1 but as v1.3.0. Due to the lack of a patch level indicator in the 
                           v1.2 release, the IntelliJ IDEA plugin frameworks was not seeing v1.2.1-2020.1 as being newer than
                           v1.2-2020.1 and therefore not auto updating to it. Moving forward, all releases will have a patch level
                           configured to prevent this issue.<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.2.1</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Fixed <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/64'>issue #64</a> in which a plugin 
                           'State Error' exception may have occurred on IDE startup.<br>
        <br>
        <strong>v1.2</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Enhanced the Subsystem "Create as Singleton" option to offer different Singleton initialization 
                           methodologies (based on the methodologies presented in the <em>Geeks for Geeks</em> 
                           <a href="https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/singleton-design-pattern">Singleton Design Pattern</a> article).<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Added functionality to Command class creation so that Subsystems that are Singletons are not added 
                           as parameters to the Command's constructor, but rather are initialized in their field declaration
                           via a call to their singleton getter method (or field if applicable).<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Enhanced the Command class creation dialog so that abstract subsystem classes are not listed in
                           the "required subsystems" selection pane. Since an abstract subsystem cannot be instantiated, it
                           made no sense to present them as an option in the list.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Enhanced the component creation dialogs so that the last selected base component is remembered 
                           and pre-selected on the next use.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Implemented <a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/63'>Feature #63</a>: 
                           Auto reimport gradle project when changes are made to <em>vendordeps</em> directory so that changes are 
                           picked up and the project classpath is updated appropriately. 
                           (<a href='https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/61'>Feature #61</a>, UI for 
                           adding and managing <em>vendordeps</em>, is still pending.)<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Some miscellaneous internal improvements.<br>
        <br>
        
        <strong>v1.1</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Added an action (<em>Tools > FRC > Check for WPI Lib Update</em>) to check for the availability of a WPI Lib update. The action runs 
                           automatically when an FRC project is opened, and then periodically in the background while the FRC project is open.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Fixed the auto clear feature in the rioLog console tool window. It was keying on an old startup message and thus not working.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Removed the print action from the rioLog console. It was likely never used and was using real estate and adding clutter.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Rearranged the order of the action buttons on the rioLog console so that the more frequently used actions are
                           on the top to improve usability when the tool window height is reduced.<br>
        <br>
        
        <strong>v1.0</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Dropping the zero based versioning and migrating to a 1.0 version after 14 such releases over the course of three years.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Improvements to the new FRC Robot Project Wizard<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Wizard automatically creates Gradle build and deploy Run Configurations, as well as debugger attachment Configurations.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Added 2020 project and example templates.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; The wizard checks for the latest WPI Lib version so new projects always can use the latest version.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; RioLog Console reads team number from project level rather than application level.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Added JSON Schema Validation for the wpilib_preferences.json file. This prevents errors and provides auto completion.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Major rewrite of the FRC class creation template framework to make them more robust and convenient.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Additional words added to the FRC spellcheck dictionary.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Miscellaneous changes and improvements<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Deprecated the custom FrcModuleType used by the custom FRC Project Wizard and instead have the wizard create JavaModuleType projects.
        This change will have very minimal impact to users, but improves some functionality. See <a href="https://gitlab.com/Javaru/frc-intellij-idea-plugin/issues/41">Enhancement #41</a>
        for additional details.<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Good luck to all FRC teams in the 2020 <em>INFINITE RECHARGE</em> game.<br>
        <br>
        
        <strong>v0.1 - v0.8.1</strong> <br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&bull; Fourteen releases over three years containing numerous features, enhancements, and fixes.
    ]]>
    </change-notes>

    
